<linker>
  <!--
    Managed Stripping Level is set to High. IL2CPP strips any method it cannot
    prove is reachable from static analysis of the IL.

    VContainer instantiates every registered type through reflection —
    VContainer/Runtime/Internal/ReflectionInjector.cs:

        injectTypeInfo.InjectConstructor.ConstructorInfo.Invoke(parameterValues)

    There is no direct `new` for our systems anywhere in the source, so the
    stripper removes their constructors and the container throws at runtime.
    This never reproduces in the Editor (Mono, no stripping) — only on device.

    VContainer's source generator would emit "<TypeName>GeneratedInjector"
    classes that IL2CPP *can* trace (see InjectorCache.GetOrBuild), which would
    make this file unnecessary. It is not shipped in the git-URL distribution
    we install from, so we are on the reflection path and preserve explicitly.

    UniTask and DOTween are intentionally absent: UniTask uses no reflection,
    and DOTween marks its own reflection entry points with [Preserve].
  -->
  <assembly fullname="VContainer" preserve="all" />
  <assembly fullname="TurretRush.Game" preserve="all" />
</linker>
